IMPORT prelude

-- International Development Association Act 2002 (Singapore) -- the Government's subscription limits (s 4(2), (3)), the notes the
-- Minister may issue in place of payment (s 5(1)), the Companies Act 1967 not applying to the Association or its securities (s 9),
-- and the parts of Article VIII of the Agreement that s 8(1) gives the force of law, as a person dealing with the Association meets
-- them: who may sue the Association and where (Article VIII s 3), seizure of its property (ss 3, 4), the immunities of its personnel
-- (s 8), and taxation of the Association, of its staff's salaries and of its securities (s 9) read with the s 8(2) limits.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/IDAA2002.txt. The cover says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the deposit's
-- footer reads "Informal Consolidation – version in force from 23/12/2022". The latest amendment annotated in the body is
-- "[Act 34 of 2022 wef 23/12/2022]" (on s 4(1)-(3)); s 4(1) also carries "[10/2004]". The Legislative History (not part of the Act)
-- lists Act 34 of 2022, the International Development Association (Amendment) Act 2022, commencement 23 December 2022, as the
-- latest entry. The arrangement of sections and the body agree (ss 1-10 and the Schedule).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0177 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. For a person, the answer is mostly the Schedule: whether they can sue the Association, whether its
-- officials can be sued, whether an Association salary or Association bond interest can be taxed.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: acceptance of the Agreement (s 3), the Consolidated Fund charges (ss 4(1), 5(2), 6(2), 7), the loan power (s 6(1)),
-- the Minister's powers to amend the Schedule and make regulations (ss 8(3), 10), and Article VIII ss 1, 2, 5, 6, 7 and 10 (stated in
-- comments only). The Agreement beyond Article VIII, and the membership resolution, are not deposited.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `International Development Association Act 2002 -- immunities and subscription`

§§ `4(2), (3) -- the Government's subscription`

-- s 4(2): "Subject to subsection (3), the total subscription to the Association must not exceed the sum of one million United States
-- dollars unless increased with the approval of Parliament signified by resolution."
-- s 4(3): "Any additional subscription made on any occasion on behalf of the Government to the Association by reason of Singapore's
-- membership ... must be authorised by, and must not exceed the maximum amount specified in, a resolution of Parliament for that
-- occasion."
-- Amounts are in US$ millions. INFERENCE: s 4(2) and s 4(3) are read as two separate tests, both to be met; the text does not say
-- how "Subject to subsection (3)" reconciles them beyond that.
GIVEN `total subscription in US$ millions` IS A NUMBER, `Parliament has approved an increase by resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the total subscription is within s 4(2)` IF
        `total subscription in US$ millions` AT MOST 1
    OR  `Parliament has approved an increase by resolution`

GIVEN `additional subscription in US$ millions` IS A NUMBER,
      `a resolution of Parliament for that occasion exists` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `maximum in the resolution in US$ millions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the additional subscription is within s 4(3)` IF
        `a resolution of Parliament for that occasion exists`
    AND `additional subscription in US$ millions` AT MOST `maximum in the resolution in US$ millions`

§§ `5(1) -- notes in place of payment`

-- s 5(1): "To the extent to which the Association is prepared to accept from the Government notes or other obligations that are
-- non-interest bearing and non-negotiable and that are payable at their par value on demand in place of any payment ... under
-- section 4, the Minister may, with the concurrence of the President under Article 144(1) of the Constitution, create and issue to
-- the Association ... any such notes or other obligations."
GIVEN `the Association is prepared to accept the note` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the note bears interest` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the note is negotiable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the note is payable at par on demand` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the President concurs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may issue the note` IF
        `the Association is prepared to accept the note`
    AND (NOT `the note bears interest`)
    AND (NOT `the note is negotiable`)
    AND `the note is payable at par on demand`
    AND `the President concurs`

§§ `9 -- the Companies Act does not apply`

-- s 9: "The Association is not to be regarded as a corporation within the meaning of the Companies Act 1967, and the provisions of
-- that Act do not apply to the Association or to the issue by the Association of any shares, debentures, bonds, notes or other
-- securities."
GIVEN `the issuer is the Association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Companies Act 1967 applies to the issue` IF
    NOT `the issuer is the Association`

§§ `Schedule, Article VIII section 3 -- suing the Association`

-- Art VIII s 2: full juridical personality; capacity "to contract", to acquire and dispose of property, "to institute legal
-- proceedings".
-- Art VIII s 3: "Actions may be brought against the Association only in a court of competent jurisdiction in the territories of a
-- member in which the Association has an office, has appointed an agent for the purpose of accepting service or notice of process, or
-- has issued or guaranteed securities. No actions shall, however, be brought by members or persons acting for or deriving claims from
-- members."
-- Unlike a general immunity, s 3 sets no limit on the KIND of claim: any claimant who is not a member (or acting for or deriving from
-- one) may sue, if the venue condition is met. The Schedule as deposited carries no general waiver article; s 8(2) of the Act does
-- not add one. Whether the Association has an office or agent in Singapore is not in the deposit, so it is a parameter.
DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `a claim on the Association's borrowing`
    `a supplier's claim for the price of goods`
    `an employee's claim for wages`
    `a claim for personal injury on Association premises`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim,
      `the claimant is a member or acts for or derives a claim from one` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Association has an office, agent or securities in that territory` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the court has competent jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action may be brought against the Association` IF
        (NOT `the claimant is a member or acts for or derives a claim from one`)
    AND `the Association has an office, agent or securities in that territory`
    AND `the court has competent jurisdiction`

§§ `Schedule, Article VIII sections 3 and 4 -- seizing the Association's property`

-- Art VIII s 3 (last sentence): property and assets "shall, wheresoever located and by whomsoever held, be immune from all forms of
-- seizure, attachment or execution before the delivery of final judgment against the Association".
-- Art VIII s 4: they "shall be immune from search, requisition, confiscation, expropriation or any other form of seizure by executive
-- or legislative action".
-- Not encoded: s 5 (archives "inviolable"), s 6 (assets free from restrictions, regulations, controls and moratoria "To the extent
-- necessary to carry out the operations"), s 7 (official communications treated as other members' are), s 10 (members to make the
-- Article effective in their own law).
GIVEN `final judgment has been delivered against the Association` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the seizure is by executive or legislative action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Association's property may be seized` IF
        `final judgment has been delivered against the Association`
    AND (NOT `the seizure is by executive or legislative action`)

§§ `Schedule, Article VIII section 8 -- Association personnel`

-- Art VIII s 8: "All Governors, Executive Directors, Alternates, officers and employees of the Association -- (i) shall be immune from
-- legal process with respect to acts performed by them in their official capacity except when the Association waives this immunity;
-- (ii) not being local nationals, shall be accorded the same immunities from immigration restrictions, alien registration
-- requirements and national service obligations and the same facilities as regards exchange restrictions as are accorded by members
-- to the representatives, officials and employees of comparable rank of other members; (iii) shall be granted the same treatment in
-- respect of travelling facilities ...".
-- Experts and consultants on missions are not named; a consultant who is not an officer or employee is treated as outside s 8.
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `a Governor`
    `an Executive Director`
    `an Alternate`
    `an officer`
    `an employee`
    `a consultant who is not an employee`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is section 8 personnel` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a consultant who is not an employee` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the act was in official capacity` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Association has waived the immunity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is immune from legal process for the act` IF
        `the person is section 8 personnel` `the person`
    AND `the act was in official capacity`
    AND (NOT `the Association has waived the immunity`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the person is a local national` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person gets the immigration and national service immunities` IF
        `the person is section 8 personnel` `the person`
    AND (NOT `the person is a local national`)

§§ `Schedule, Article VIII section 9(a) and s 8(2) -- taxation of the Association`

-- Art VIII s 9(a): "The Association, its assets, property, income and its operations and transactions authorised by this Agreement,
-- shall be immune from all taxation and from all customs duties. The Association shall also be immune from liability for the
-- collection or payment of any tax or duty."
-- s 8(2): "Nothing in section 9 of Article VIII of the Agreement is to be construed as -- (a) entitling the Association to import into
-- Singapore goods free of any duty of customs without any restriction on their subsequent sale in Singapore; or (b) conferring on the
-- Association any exemption from taxes or duties which are no more than charges for services rendered."
-- s 8(2) has only these two limbs: it does not carve out taxes forming part of the price of goods sold. INFERENCE: on the words, a
-- tax passed on in the price of goods sold to the Association falls within "all taxation"; whether the immunity reaches a tax that is
-- legally the seller's is not settled by the text. Duty-free import where the later sale IS restricted is read from (a) (inference
-- from "without any restriction").
DECLARE Levy IS ONE OF
    `income tax on the Association's income`
    `customs duty on goods imported with a restriction on resale`
    `customs duty on goods imported with no restriction on resale`
    `a tax forming part of the price of goods sold to the Association`
    `a charge for services rendered dressed as a tax`
    `a duty to collect tax from the Association's payments`

GIVEN `the levy` IS A Levy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Association is exempt from the levy` IF
    CONSIDER `the levy`
    WHEN `customs duty on goods imported with no restriction on resale` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a charge for services rendered dressed as a tax` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Schedule, Article VIII section 9(b) -- salaries paid by the Association`

-- Art VIII s 9(b): "No tax shall be levied on or in respect of salaries and emoluments paid by the Association to Executive Directors,
-- Alternates, officials or employees of the Association who are not local citizens, local subjects, or other local nationals."
-- Governors are named in s 8 but NOT in s 9(b). "officials" in s 9(b) is read to include the "officers" of s 8 (inference).
-- A local citizen or national gets no exemption at all; no member declaration is needed to tax them.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is named in section 9(b)` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a Governor` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a consultant who is not an employee` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the person is a local citizen, subject or national` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9(b) bars tax on the Association salary` IF
        `the person is named in section 9(b)` `the person`
    AND (NOT `the person is a local citizen, subject or national`)

§§ `Schedule, Article VIII section 9(c), (d) -- Association bonds`

-- Art VIII s 9(c): no taxation "of any kind" on any obligation or security ISSUED by the Association "(including any dividend or
-- interest thereon) by whomsoever held -- (i) which discriminates against such obligation or security solely because it is issued by
-- the Association; or (ii) if the sole jurisdictional basis for such taxation is the place or currency in which it is issued, made
-- payable or paid, or the location of any office or place of business maintained by the Association."
-- Art VIII s 9(d): the same for a security GUARANTEED by the Association, but (ii) names only "the location of any office or place of
-- business maintained by the Association".
DECLARE Basis IS ONE OF
    `the holder's residence`
    `the place of issue`
    `the currency of issue`
    `the place of payment`
    `the location of an Association office`

GIVEN `the basis` IS A Basis, `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the basis is a forbidden sole basis` IF
    CONSIDER `the basis`
    WHEN `the location of an Association office` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the place of issue` THEN `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Association`
    WHEN `the currency of issue` THEN `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Association`
    WHEN `the place of payment` THEN `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Association`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the basis` IS A Basis,
      `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Association` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the basis is the sole jurisdictional basis` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the tax discriminates solely because of the Association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9 bars the tax on the security` IF
        `the tax discriminates solely because of the Association`
    OR  (`the basis is the sole jurisdictional basis` AND `the basis is a forbidden sole basis` `the basis` `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Association`)
